# Orchestration artifacts

Full contracts: [`orchestrator.md`](../agents/orchestrator.md), [`planner.md`](../agents/planner.md), [`builder.md`](../agents/builder.md), [`tester.md`](../agents/tester.md), [`validator.md`](../agents/validator.md). Per-agent Cursor rules: [`orchestrator.mdc`](./orchestrator.mdc), [`planner.mdc`](./planner.mdc), [`builder.mdc`](./builder.mdc), [`tester.mdc`](./tester.mdc), [`validator.mdc`](./validator.mdc). Index: [`.cursor/agents/INDEX.md`](../agents/INDEX.md).

**Templates** ([`../orchestrations/_template/`](../orchestrations/_template/)): `task-manifest.json`, `plan.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`, `test-matrix.md`, `build-log.md`, `test-report.md`, `validation-report.md`, `human-approval.md`, and [`README.md`](../orchestrations/_template/README.md) (copy into `{task-id}/` when bootstrapping). Cross-cutting audit: [`docs/validation-checklist.md`](../docs/validation-checklist.md). Test layers: [`docs/test-matrix-template.md`](../docs/test-matrix-template.md).

## Path

Runs live under **`.cursor/orchestrations/{task-id}/`**. Do not treat orchestration files as application source — they record pipeline state and stage outputs.

## `task-manifest.json` — Orchestrator only

- **Only the Orchestrator** (or a human following the same contract) may create or update **`task-manifest.json`**.
- **Planner, Builder, Tester, and Validator** must **not** edit the manifest — read-only for `task_id`, `objective`, `locked_artifacts`, `loop_count`, etc.
- Manifest fields such as `risk_tier`, `gate_status`, `completed_stages`, `rework_count`, `rework_history`, `session_counts`, `command_evidence`, `flags`, and `human_approval` are Orchestrator-owned routing and audit state. Other agents report facts in their owned artifact; the Orchestrator mirrors summaries into the manifest when routing.

## Per-stage writes (under `{task-id}/`)

See [`.cursor/agents/INDEX.md`](../agents/INDEX.md) (Run State table). Summary: Orchestrator → manifest + Gate 6 `human-approval.md`; Planner → plan/ACs/(planned) test-matrix; Builder → `build-log.md` only; Tester → `test-report.md` + actual test-matrix; Validator → `validation-report.md` only.

## Locks and scope

- **`locked_artifacts`:** treat listed paths as read-only unless the manifest is updated to unlock (Orchestrator/human).
- **Do not** expand scope via orchestration edits — `plan.md` is design truth; deviations belong in **`build-log.md`** under **Deviations from plan**.

## Pipeline

Default order: **Orchestrator → Planner → Builder → Tester → Validator → Orchestrator** (human approval / loops per Orchestrator rules). After editing artifacts, align with the manifest’s **`current_agent`** and completed-stage contracts before invoking the next agent. Validator **FAIL** and human `rejected_rework` outcomes return to Builder, then continue through Tester and Validator unless the Orchestrator routes back to Planner for a scope-changing rework.

## Merge-ready (do not conflate with stage completion)

**Lifecycle gates 0–6** (`gate_status` in the manifest) track pipeline stages; **merge-ready checks** (**MG-01**–**MG-05**) are the merge bar — see [validation checklist — gate mapping](../docs/validation-checklist.md#lifecycle-gates-merge-ready-gates-and-gate_status).

**Merge-ready** claims are governed by [workflow-gates.mdc](./workflow-gates.mdc) (ADR + alignment gaps + `validation-report.md` + `test-report.md` + tooling). Stage artifacts alone are insufficient: Builder/Tester must not assert merge-ready; Orchestrator uses `awaiting_human` only after Validator **PASS** / **PASS_WITH_NOTES** and applicable MG gates; `complete` requires **lifecycle Gate 6** human approval in the manifest.
